  "answer": "Not all checks pass. The build passed, but the unit tests failed, so the component stage was skipped. I didn't modify any files.\n\n| Stage | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `build` | passed |\n| `unit` | **failed** (exit code 2): 39 of 272 tests failed, 233 passed |\n| `component` | skipped because the run stopped early |\n| integration and skills stages | not part of the configured verification run |\n\nAll 39 failures have one cause: `SemanticMatcher.Apply` throws `ArgumentException` for matcher names it should recognize. The unit log's `Failed` lines add up to 78 because each failing test appears twice.\n\nThe error message is:\n```\nSystem.ArgumentException : Unknown semantic matcher 'isnull' for field 'deletedAt'\n   at ConfIT.Matching.SemanticMatcher.Apply(...) in src/ConfIT/Matching/SemanticMatcher.cs:line 61\n```\nThe rejected names are all lowercase: `isnull`, `isuuid`, `isnotnull`, `greaterthan` and `lessthan`. The built-in matchers are camelCase (`isUuid`, `isIsoDate`, `isEmail`). That suggests the lookup at line 61 of `SemanticMatcher.cs` no longer matches names case-insensitively, or the lowercased name is checked against a case-sensitive table. I haven't opened that file to confirm.\n\nThe failures are in two test classes:\n- **`SemanticMatcherTests`:** 33 tests across all the named matchers (`isUuid`, `isEmail`, `isIsoDate`/`isIsoDateTime`, `isNull`/`isNotNull`, `isEmpty`/`isNotEmpty`, `hasLength`, `greaterThan`/`lessThan`), plus the custom-matcher and nested-path cases.\n- **`ResultMatcherTests`:** 6 tests, because `ResultMatcher` calls `SemanticMatcher`:\n  - `MatchResponseBody_NullExpectedWithSemanticMatcher_DoesNotThrow`\n  - `MatchResponseBody_AllThreeMatcherTypes_EachApplied`\n  - `MatchResponseBody_SemanticMatcherFails_ReturnedDescriptionNamesField`\n  - `MatchResponseBody_SemanticMatcherValid_PassesAndRemovesField`\n  - `MatchResponseBody_CustomMatcher_PassesForValidValue`\n  - one more with the same error\n\nTwo of these tests expect something else:\n- `Apply_FieldAbsentFromResponse_ThrowsInvalidOperationException` expected `InvalidOperationException` but got `ArgumentException`. The unknown-matcher check fires before the field-absent check.\n- `Apply_NullExpected_DoesNotThrow` and `MatchResponseBody_NullExpectedWithSemanticMatcher_DoesNotThrow` expected no exception, but got the same `ArgumentException`.\n\nThe full log is at `tmp/verification/20261021T073010Z-ce9259/unit.log`.",
